{"page_content": "ACME/Flame Design Final Report (2023) \n \n6 April 2023 \n106 \n \n \nIn 2021, Flame Design Co-Investigator Peter Sunderland was inducted as a Fellow of the Combustion \nInstitute for his \u201csignificant contributions to understanding laminar flame dynamics and soot \nformation and oxidation.\u201d \n \nAdditional awards include the following, where images of the award certificate and journal cover from \nitem #5 appear subsequently: \n5.  Award for Gravitational and Space Research Journal Cover, Flame Ignition in Space, Jan. 2021.  \n4.  Third Prize, Art Competition, 5th U.S. Combustion Meeting, San Diego, 2007.  \n3.  Finalist, Science and Engineering Visualization Challenge, National Science Foundation, 2006.  \n2.  Third Prize, Art Competition, 30th International Symposium on Combustion, 2004.  \n1.  Best-Paper Award, Northern Ohio section of AIAA, 2003. \n \n \nCertificate for the winning Flame Design entry, Flame Ignition in Space, in the 2020 Art Competition \nof the American Society for Gravitational and Space Research (ASGSR).", "metadata": {"source": "PSI-10_Reports_FinalRpt_ACMEFlameDesign.pdf", "page": 106}}